<section class="content-page legal-page"><div class="nb-wrap">
<p class="eyebrow">NeonLib · Privacy</p><h1>Request deletion of NeonLib data</h1>
<article class="legal-copy">
<p>You can request deletion of personal data held by Neon Break for the NeonLib Android app without installing the app or signing in.</p>
<h2>Send a deletion request</h2>
<ol>
<li>Email <a href="mailto:info@neonbreak.com?subject=NeonLib%20data%20deletion%20request">info@neonbreak.com</a> with the subject <strong>NeonLib data deletion request</strong>.</li>
<li>Describe which data you want deleted, such as a content report and an answer excerpt you submitted. Include the report ID if you have it. If you do not, provide the approximate submission date and the reported collection or feature so we can try to locate it.</li>
<li>We will reply to your email. We may ask for limited additional information to locate the data and verify that the request concerns you. Do not send passwords, API keys, identity documents or your whole document library.</li>
</ol>
<p><a class="button button-primary" href="mailto:info@neonbreak.com?subject=NeonLib%20data%20deletion%20request">Email a deletion request</a></p>
<p>If the button does not open an email app, copy the address above into your email service. Requests are handled manually. We aim to respond and act on valid requests within one month; if an applicable exception or permitted extension is needed, we will explain the reason and expected timeframe.</p>
<h2>What we delete or retain</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Server-held reports:</strong> identifiable personal information in your report explanation, included answer excerpt and associated personal moderation notes can be requested for deletion. We will explain if we cannot identify a record from the information available.</li>
<li><strong>Routine report retention:</strong> open reports are kept while investigated. Closed reports and associated personal moderation notes are scheduled by policy for deletion 90 days after closure. This is currently a manual process. A deletion request is assessed separately; you do not have to wait for the 90-day period.</li>
<li><strong>Exceptions:</strong> necessary information may be retained to meet a legal obligation or handle an active dispute, until that obligation or dispute no longer requires it. We will explain any applicable exception in our response. Records with personal information irreversibly removed may be retained.</li>
<li><strong>Technical logs and backups:</strong> eligible identifiable records are included in our assessment. Restricted backup copies may expire separately under the backup lifecycle, and security records may be retained while necessary to investigate an incident or meet a legal obligation. We will explain applicable retention for your request.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Delete data stored on your phone</h2>
<p>We cannot remotely erase your local library. To remove all local NeonLib data, open <strong>Android Settings → Apps → NeonLib → Storage → Clear storage / Clear data</strong>. Labels vary by device. This removes the app's local notes, imported documents, indexes, settings and other app data. Save anything you want to keep first.</p>
<p>Original documents outside the app, exported files and Android or device-provider backups require separate deletion. Clearing local storage does not withdraw reports already submitted to our server.</p>
<h2>Optional online AI and publisher accounts</h2>
<p>If you sent content directly to an online AI provider using your own API key, contact that provider to request deletion of information it holds. We cannot administer your external provider account.</p>
<p>The Android app does not require a NeonLib account. If your request concerns a separate NeonLib publisher account created on our website, mention that in your email and send it from the account email address where possible. We will explain the verification and deletion steps for that account.</p>
<p>NeonLib is operated by Web Solutions, obrt za informatičke usluge, vl. Goran Sambolić, under the Neon Break brand. See the <a href="<?php echo esc_url( home_url( '/neonlib/privacy-policy/' ) ); ?>">NeonLib Privacy Policy</a> for details.</p>
